    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing a basic Island when Command Tower or Grixis Panorama would be strictly better. Command Tower taps for any color in a Grixis (UBR) deck, providing more flexible mana. Grixis Panorama can fetch any basic Island/Swamp/Mountain later. With Cascade Bluffs and Smoldering Marsh already providing UR colors, the player needs black mana most urgently (for Sever the Bloodline and Anhelo). Command Tower would provide that flexibility, and Darkwater Catacombs or Thriving Moor would also help fix for black. Playing a basic Island is the least useful land since blue is already well-covered by Cascade Bluffs.",
      "action_taken": "Played basic Island as land drop for the turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Command Tower to have access to any color (especially black for Sever the Bloodline and Anhelo), or play Thriving Moor (choosing blue or red) to fix black mana while keeping Command Tower for a future turn when multiple colors are needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 48,
      "player": "Haiku ESPN",
      "decision_index": 37,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Plains instead of Command Tower wastes flexibility. Command Tower produces any color in the commander's identity (at least WUB), making it strictly better than Plains for an untapped land drop. Playing Command Tower now preserves the basic Plains for later, where basics have advantages (fetchable, immune to nonbasic hate). The player's reasoning about 'paying for Phantom Steed' is also confused since Phantom Steed is already on the battlefield.",
      "action_taken": "Played Plains as their land drop for turn 3.",
      "better_line": "Play Command Tower instead, preserving the basic Plains for a future land drop where being a basic is relevant.",
