      "decision_index": 52,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Monologue Tax before playing a land is a sequencing error. Gem3F Libby has Secluded Steppe and Plains in hand, and only 3 lands on the battlefield. Playing a land first (Plains) would allow casting Commander's Sphere instead, which provides mana acceleration and card draw potential. Alternatively, playing the land first is simply correct sequencing - you should always play your land before casting spells in case you draw into something or need the information. More importantly, Commander's Sphere would ramp them toward their expensive cards (Duplicant at 6, Hellkite Tyrant at 6) while Monologue Tax is a relatively low-impact enchantment in multiplayer that only triggers on opponents' second spells each turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Monologue Tax for 2W using all three lands, without first making a land drop.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains first (making a land drop), then cast Commander's Sphere for 3 mana to accelerate toward the powerful 6-drops in hand (Duplicant, Hellkite Tyrant). Monologue Tax could be played next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 65,
      "player": "Gem3F Libby",
      "decision_index": 61,
    },
