    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Oath of Druids triggers at each player's upkeep, allowing a player who controls fewer creatures than an opponent to reveal cards until they find a creature. Sonnet Timmy currently controls 0 creatures while Gem25F Analyst has Phantom Steed and Wayfarer's Bauble (Phantom Steed is a creature), and Haiku ESPN has Spellbinding Soprano. However, Oath of Druids benefits ALL players symmetrically - any opponent with fewer creatures than another opponent can also use it. In a 4-player game, this is extremely risky as it helps opponents cheat creatures into play too. Additionally, Sonnet Timmy should consider playing the land (Azorius Chancery or Homeward Path) before casting spells to have more mana available and better sequencing. The Azorius Chancery entering tapped means it should be played sooner rather than later. Playing the land first is generally correct sequencing.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Oath of Druids for 1G before playing a land for the turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Homeward Path (or Azorius Chancery bouncing a Forest) first, then cast Oath of Druids. More importantly, Oath of Druids in a multiplayer game is very risky as it benefits all players symmetrically. However, if Sonnet Timmy's deck has powerful creatures to find, it could be worthwhile. The land-before-spell sequencing is the clearer minor error.",
      "type": "blunder",
