      "player": "Gem3F Libby",
      "decision_index": 320,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Hellkite Tyrant is a massive threat that steals all artifacts on combat damage. Sonnet Timmy has Swords to Plowshares in hand and an untapped Plains to cast it. The Hellkite Tyrant could steal artifacts from any player it hits, and as a 6/5 flyer with trample, it's very hard to block. Letting it resolve when you have a 1-mana instant removal spell available is a significant mistake. While Sonnet Timmy doesn't have many artifacts themselves, other players do (Monologue Tax/Thousand-Year Elixir for Libby, Cataclysmic Gearhulk for Analyst, Rakdos Signet for Haiku), and the 6/5 flying trampler is a serious clock. More importantly, Swords to Plowshares can be cast in response to the creature entering the battlefield or during combat before damage, but removing it now before it can attack is cleanest.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to respond to Hellkite Tyrant being cast/entering, letting it resolve onto the battlefield.",
      "better_line": "Cast Swords to Plowshares targeting Hellkite Tyrant to exile it immediately. It's a 6/5 flying trampler that steals artifacts on combat damage - one of the most dangerous creatures in the game and well worth a premium removal spell.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 232,
      "player": "Sonnet Timmy",
      "decision_index": 326,
    },
