      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3F Libby is at 3 life and Sonnet Timmy has Treacherous Terrain in hand, which deals damage to each opponent equal to the number of lands they control. Libby controls 8 lands (Forgotten Cave, Plains, Mountain, Plains, Plains, Plains + Monologue Tax and Thousand-Year Elixir are not lands, so 6 lands). Actually counting carefully: Forgotten Cave, Plains, Mountain, Plains, Plains, Plains = 6 lands. That's 6 damage to Libby who is at 3 life - lethal. Treacherous Terrain costs {6}{R}{G} = 8 mana. Sonnet Timmy has Forest, Forest, Azorius Chancery, Plains, Mountain, Homeward Path, Command Tower = produces at most G+G+WU+W+R+C+any = 7 mana with the right colors but needs 8 total (6 generic + R + G). Let me recount: Forest (G), Forest (G), Azorius Chancery (WU), Plains (W), Mountain (R), Homeward Path (C), Command Tower (any) = G+G+W+U+W+R+C+any. That's 8 mana total. Treacherous Terrain costs {6}{R}{G} = 8 mana. With Command Tower producing G, we'd have G, G, W, U, W, R, C, G = R and G covered, plus 6 generic from the rest. That's exactly 8 mana! But several lands are tapped: Forest (tapped), Azorius Chancery (tapped), Mountain (tapped), Command Tower (tapped). Untapped: Forest, Plains, Homeward Path. That's only 3 mana available (G, W, C). Not enough to cast Treacherous Terrain. So Treacherous Terrain can't be cast... wait, it IS showing as a choice option. The game is offering it as choice. Let me recheck - the choice says 'Treacherous Terrain {6}{R}{G} [Cast]' is available. If the game engine is offering it, Timmy has the mana. But looking at untapped lands: Forest (untapped), Plains (untapped), Homeward Path (untapped) = only 3 mana. That shouldn't be enough. Actually wait - the Lightning Rager token exists from Rite of the Raging Storm. It will be sacrificed at end step anyway. This doesn't affect mana. Hmm, maybe I'm misreading tapped status. Let me recheck the board more carefully. The tapped lands for Sonnet Timmy are: Forest (tapped), Azorius Chancery (tapped), Mountain (tapped), Command Tower (tapped). Untapped: Forest, Plains, Homeward Path = G + W + C = 3 mana. The game offering Treacherous Terrain as castable seems wrong, or maybe there's something I'm missing. If it IS actually castable and the game engine confirms it, then declining is a major blunder since it kills Libby at 3 life. But with only 3 mana available, it shouldn't be castable. I'll trust the game engine that it's a valid option since it's listed as [Cast].",
      "action_taken": "Declined to take any action, passing without casting Treacherous Terrain which was offered as a castable spell.",
      "better_line": "Cast Treacherous Terrain to deal lethal damage to Gem3F Libby (at 3 life with 6+ lands) and significant damage to other opponents. If the game engine is correctly offering this as castable, it eliminates a player.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 349,
      "player": "Sonnet Timmy",
      "decision_index": 1457,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gave Akroan Horse to Gem3F Libby who is at 3 life and likely to die very soon. When Libby is eliminated, the Akroan Horse leaves the game, ending the token production. Haiku ESPN at 18 life would keep the Horse alive much longer, generating more 1/1 Soldier tokens for Sonnet Timmy over multiple turns.",
      "action_taken": "Gave Akroan Horse to Gem3F Libby (3 life)",
      "better_line": "Give Akroan Horse to Haiku ESPN (18 life) to maximize the number of upkeeps generating Soldier tokens, since ESPN is far more likely to survive longer.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 349,
      "player": "Sonnet Timmy",
      "decision_index": 1457,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Libby blocked a 5/1 trample Lightning Rager with Jor Kadeen, the Prevailer (8/4) instead of Akroan Horse (3/4). Both blockers have 4 toughness, so both result in only 1 trample damage getting through. However, Jor Kadeen dies to 5 damage (only 4 toughness) and is by far the most valuable creature on Libby's board (8/4 with metalcraft boosting all creatures). Akroan Horse is a 0/4 defender that was given to Libby by an opponent - losing it is nearly free.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked the Lightning Rager with Jor Kadeen, the Prevailer, losing their best creature",
      "better_line": "Block with Akroan Horse (3/4 defender) - same 1 trample damage gets through, but preserves the much more valuable Jor Kadeen",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 352,
      "player": "Gem3F Libby",
      "decision_index": 1462,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose to add {RR} from Cascade Bluffs instead of {UR}, despite their own reasoning indicating they wanted {UR}. With cards like Talrand's Invocation, Extravagant Replication, and Dread Summons in hand that all require blue mana, having access to blue mana when floating before River's Rebuke resolves would have been more useful.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Cascade Bluffs to add {RR}",
      "better_line": "Activate Cascade Bluffs to add {UR} to have access to blue mana for replaying bounced permanents or casting blue spells",
      "type": "blunder",
