    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With Gem3F Libby at only 3 life and Rite of the Raging Storm on the battlefield (which creates a 5/1 Lightning Rager for each player at the beginning of their upkeep), Libby is likely dead soon anyway. However, casting Propaganda ({2}{U}) would provide important protection against the Lightning Rager tokens from Rite of the Raging Storm, which threaten 5 damage per turn from each opponent. With 40 life, this isn't immediately critical, but Propaganda is a strong defensive permanent that gets better the longer it's in play. Wall of Omens replaces itself and provides a 0/4 blocker, which is reasonable, but Propaganda would tax all opponents' attacks going forward. The decision is close - Wall of Omens cantrips and blocks, while Propaganda provides broader protection. Additionally, casting Wall of Omens before combat with Sefris as commander (W/U/B) could be relevant for dungeon venturing if Sefris were in play, but she appears to be in the command zone. The play is defensible since the cantrip digs for answers.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Wall of Omens for {1}{W} to draw a card and get a 0/4 blocker",
      "better_line": "Cast Propaganda for {2}{U} to tax attackers, particularly the 5/1 Lightning Rager tokens from Rite of the Raging Storm that threaten significant damage each turn cycle",
